1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:05,290
Every chapter runs on an exact quantum simulator, right in your browser.

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:07,380
You do not read about superposition:

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,927
you build it, measure it, and watch interference cancel.

4
00:00:11,687 --> 00:00:16,257
At the heart of Shor's algorithm is the quantum Fourier transform.

5
00:00:16,257 --> 00:00:19,867
Step through the real gate circuit, one gate at a time,

6
00:00:19,867 --> 00:00:24,017
and watch a repeating pattern turn into sharp peaks.

7
00:00:24,787 --> 00:00:26,973
Then factor fifteen end to end:

8
00:00:26,973 --> 00:00:32,992
superposition, modular exponentiation, the Fourier transform, continued fractions,

9
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:36,438
and out come the factors, three times five.

10
00:00:37,187 --> 00:00:38,461
Now add noise.

11
00:00:38,461 --> 00:00:43,714
On ten simulated qubits, the peaks blur, and the answer is lost.

12
00:00:43,714 --> 00:00:48,141
Real qubits fail roughly once in every thousand operations.
